# 1 blocks only 4; 2 -> 3 -> 4 is a chain. Prerequisites-first alone would put the
# lone blocker first (lowest id among the roots), hanging its lane open beside the
# whole chain. Nothing forces that: it need only precede 4, and sliding it down to
# just above 4 costs the chain one row and saves it two.
new "Lone blocker" --id aaaaaaa --empty
new "Chain head" --id bbbbbbb --empty
new "Chain middle" --id ccccccc --requires bbbbbbb --empty
new "Chain tail" --id ddddddd --requires aaaaaaa,ccccccc --empty
